  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Systems to End the Malaria Burden through Meaningful Engagement - II (SEMBE II)</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="FR">Syst&#xe8;mes pour mettre fin au fardeau du paludisme gr&#xe2;ce &#xe0; un engagement significatif - II (SEMBE II)</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="FR">Syst&#xe8;mes pour mettre fin au fardeau du paludisme gr&#xe2;ce &#xe0; un engagement significatif - II (SEMBE II)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">(Cameroon):  ...The SEMBE-II award is one of two bilateral mechanisms (also see SEMBE-I, #111632) designed to support the Cameroonian government and local stakeholders to lead disease control and prevention efforts. The SEMBE-II mechanism will provide technical assistance at central level and strengthen the capacity of health service providers and community health workers to deliver case management services, strengthen community-based disease surveillance, and implement SBC strategies and SMC in the North Region of the country. This mechanism may expand activities to other regions based on epidemiological data and the donor landscape. Planned interventions will include:.. .Designing, implementing, and monitoring innovative, evidence-based, high-quality      interventions that will support the prevention, diagnosis, and treatment      of malaria at regional and district levels.Training healthcare providers on integrated disease surveillance, event-based      surveillance, and ensuring that community-level reporting is effective.Implementing annual SMC campaigns during peak transmission season in the North Region.Providing technical support to the NMCP at central, regional, district, health      facility, and community levels to increase access to quality malaria data      and utilization. Promoting infection prevention and control (IPC) practices at health facility and      community levels.Ensuring the rational use of antimalarial drugs and other antimicrobials to      minimize AMR.. ..This mechanism will directly contribute to Objective 1.1 of the FY 2022-2026 JSP to &quot;strengthen global health security, combat infectious disease threats, and address priority global health challenges through bilateral engagement and within multilateral fora.&quot;.. ..</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="FR">Incluez les activit&#xe9;s qui contribuent aux syst&#xe8;mes au niveau national, r&#xe9;gional ou du district en soutenant le financement, le leadership et la gouvernance (incluent de vastes efforts de r&#xe9;forme politique incluant la stigmatisation, le genre, etc.), le renforcement des capacit&#xe9;s institutionnelles, la cha&#xee;ne d&apos;approvisionnement ou les syst&#xe8;mes d&apos;approvisionnement, les programmes du Fonds mondial et la coordination des donateurs. (Veuillez noter que, comme indiqu&#xe9; dans l&apos;introduction, d&apos;autres activit&#xe9;s contribueront &#xe9;galement, &#xe0; terme, au reporting des attributions budg&#xe9;taires au RSS. Ces calculs seront trait&#xe9;s au si&#xe8;ge).</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="FR">SEMBE II est un accord de coop&#xe9;ration de cinq ans qui vise &#xe0; r&#xe9;duire consid&#xe9;rablement la morbidit&#xe9; et la mortalit&#xe9; li&#xe9;es au paludisme.</narrative>
  </description>
